 "transcript": [
  "[action] The second son laughs and dismisses his father's complaints.",
  "the second son (to Chen Fu): \"We are doing as we can, and if you wish to spend money, spend it in your land, for I have seen land in the south where the water is clear and the rice grows like grain in the field.\"",
  "Chen Fu (to the eldest son): \"I cannot go back to that town and I cannot go to the south, and I cannot walk in the fields all day and I am not like the young men. It is enough for me to be lord of the land, and to walk over it and to know its breath and its body and the breath of its people.\"",
  "[says] Chen Fu expresses his contentment with his role.",
  "[action] Chen Fu sits on the mats, satisfied.",
  "[says] (to the second son) The eldest son speaks to his brother.",
  "Chen Fu (to the eldest son): \"What now, my son?\"",
  "the eldest son (to the second son): \"It is now the time to set up a great grain market. Your grain is good and the rice grows fine in the land. We have money and we should set up a market in the town. It would be a great honor to our father.\"",
  "Chen Fu (to the eldest son): \"Well, and why not?\"",
  "[action] Chen Fu's sons leave him to discuss their plans.",
  "[action] Chen Fu sleeps in the room with the young fool.",
  "[action] (to the second son) The eldest son invites the young fool to attend the market.",
  "[action] Chen Fu sleeps beside the young fool.",
  "[action] Chen Fu and his sons arrange a large market.",
  "[action] (to the eldest son, the second son) Chen Fu and his sons set up a large market.",
  "[action] Chen Fu and his sons prepare to open the market.",
  "[action] Chen Fu and his sons set up stalls.",
  "[action] Chen Fu and his sons set up stalls.",
  "[silence] Chen Fu says nothing.",
  "[silence] the second son says nothing."
